## 6️⃣ Full Example with a Private Tile Server (OpenMapTiles)

If you have your own **OpenMapTiles** (or any MBTiles) server exposing vector tiles and a style JSON, the steps are identical – just point `style` to your own URL.

```js
const glLayer = L.maplibreGL({
  style: 'https://mytileserver.example.com/styles/streets/style.json',
  // If your server needs a token in the header:
  transformRequest: (url, resourceType) => {
    if (resourceType === 'Source' && url.includes('mytileserver')) {
      return {
        url,
        headers: { 'Authorization': 'Bearer MY_SECRET_TOKEN' }
      };
    }
  }
}).addTo(map);
```

**Tip:** If you’re serving the style from the same origin, you can omit CORS handling altogether.

